From c4b8e717be8341830ca3e17dc460368e7abef1b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:19:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): detect sleeps powerMonitor misses (clock gap)
 and absorb connect failures across a sleep/wake

On 2026-10-30 macOS sent 'resume' only at the first DarkWake after a clamshell sleep (17:08); 4.5 h of
Maintenance Sleep/DarkWake cycles and the 21:31:30 DarkWake->FullWake emitted no suspend/resume, so the
power-settle gate stayed open: reads in flight at the freeze timed out at the wake (session-mentions/outbox
after 10000ms) and pollers hit tunnels still rebuilding (Remote backend ... is down).

- PowerSettleGate.observeClock(): a 5 s unref'd ticker; a >30 s wall-clock gap = a missed sleep -> wake()
  (settle window + stagger), logged as '[power-settle] clock-gap wake'.
- absorbFailure(): a background GET whose connect failed (timeout/refused/remote down) while crossing a
  suspend or clock gap, or within 60 s of a wake, rejects as PowerSettlingError (no failure line; next poll
  retries); one summary line counts them when the grace ends. Server errors, POSTs and foreground reads are
  never absorbed.
- Tests: one per path in power-settle.test.ts (gap wake, admit notices gap, regular ticks not a wake,
  classifier, in-flight across freeze, across suspend, reconnect grace + summary, non-absorb cases, ticker
  wiring, main.ts wiring).
